WEBVTT

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:20.100
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:20.100
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:20.100
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.540
One Hundred Billion Stars, One Hundred Billion Lights

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.540
Final Chapter

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:50.690
On December 6th of Space
Year 794, Empire Year 485...

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:57.000
...while on standby in Iserlohn Fortress, Reinhard received the news of Hermann von Luneberg's death...

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:02.850
...and General HQ's approval of Luneberg's
special two-rank promotion to Admiral.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:05.790
I see.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.500
Luneberg is now...

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:14.310
I don't think Luneberg would be
pleased to have our sympathy.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:17.980
But then again, I can't be happy at the
disappearance of the "obstacle,"{i.e. Luneberg} either.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.350
Lord Reinhard probably
feels the same way.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.540
The 6th Battle of Iserlohn had
completely turned into a battle of attrition.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:35.400
But even if both sides expend all of their fleets in the battle, the Empire still has Iserlohn Fortress.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.490
In that regard, the Alliance
was at a disadvantage.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.560
Captain Yang !

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.100
If you're a Captain,
please behave like one !

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:55.100
After the blitzkrieg from a single enemy fleet had thwarted their initial plan...

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.910
...Yang felt that they
should have retreated.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.160
This is Destroyer Elf #3.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.380
We will retreat as we've
suffered some damage.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.200
There has been no casualties on this
ship, of either the captain or crew.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:12.040
Of course, the failure of the operation was
not completely determined at that point.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.670
But the path's decline to failure
was continuously increasing.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:18.400
The obvious loss of fighting personnel
goes without saying, but moreover...

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.350
...due to the number of casualties,
the hospital ships were over-extended...

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.900
...and supplies were
nearing their limit.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:26.560
You don't have
enough missiles ?

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:27.910
You don't have enough food ?

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:29.080
Oh yeah ?

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.270
Of course if you use
them, they'll be gone.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:33.010
What the heck do you
expect me to do about it ?

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.860
Despite frustration and anger,
Cazellnu did his job more than capably.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:43.960
Because of the disappearance of Vice Admiral
Cerebrese during the previous battle...

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:49.000
 ...all supply-related tasks were left to Cazellnu and he had to bear a heavy burden of responsibility.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:52.660
How are things,
Strategic Staff Officer ?

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:55.370
Will the Empire be lenient
enough to let us win the battle ?

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:56.920
No way that'll happen.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:02.400
If the enemy has one clever strategist,
we'll be in heaven when we meet again.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:05.770
Is there such a
genius in the Empire ?

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:11.080
In the past, we had great examples
like Limpao, Yusuf Tparol, and so forth.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:16.450
One hundred fifty years later it's not implausible
that the Empire has obtained their reincarnations.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.050
You're right.

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:20.350
But no matter how
talented a person is...

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:23.230
...if he doesn't have rank and authority
he can't put his talent to good use.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:27.570
At this point, the Empire seems as
atrocious as the Alliance in that department.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:31.690
In any case, they could
and should do better.

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:34.600
You always say
you hate war...

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:39.200
...but when you're on the battlefield, you
can't resist the urge to butt in, can you ?

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:44.440
No, I mean, I feel that General HQ believes
that an accumulation of personal feats...

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:48.150
...will amount to
a victory in the war.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:50.000
Is there anything
wrong with that ?

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.000
If that's the case,
there's no use for tactics.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:57.550
In some ways I think that actual battle is what provides real-life proof of tactical theories, but...

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:01.290
From my standpoint, it's economic
behavior, that of supply and demand.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.600
Unlike Yang's thoughts...

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:09.650
...there are those who aim to raise their
individual battle actions to the level of art.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:12.700
The Rosenritter are one such example.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:17.920
But besides them there are the pilots of the Spartanians, the single-seat fighter planes.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:23.370
The ones who survive write history the
way they see fit, so we can't just die easily.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.650
With those kind of reflexes, how
have you actually survived till now ?

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:34.290
I am protected by the grace
of a beautiful angel, unlike you.

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:35.550
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:39.100
I'm sure you have lots and
lots of angels on your side.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.200
Your angel last night was
a brunette, wasn't she ?

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.640
Drunk piloting is actually
against regulations, but...

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.440
Who said that ?

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:50.280
The high officials at
General Headquarters ?

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:53.280
They can actually be
sober and go to battle ?

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:55.250
I guess that's why they can
climb the social ladder so fast.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:57.840
The planes are ready !

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:58.770
All right.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:03.110
As usual, the one who shoots down the
least will buy drinks for the rest of us.

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:03.740
Yeah !

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:07.650
This is to celebrate
after our return.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:08.850
Take good care of it !

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:15.230
Launch !

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:06.100
Hey, put out the fire quickly !{give us
fire-protection suits !}

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.040
Hurry up and
extinguish the fire !

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:09.510
Yes, sir !

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:12.200
This is the Captain
of the 3rd Air Unit.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.410
We're heavily outnumbered.

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.400
Send a request to General
Headquarters for reinforcements.

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:19.250
What ?
There's no reserves ?

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:21.620
All right, I got it !

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:24.490
I'll do the fighting myself,
tell that to Headquarters !

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:27.120
Those who're well-protected
inside the walls have no clue !

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:29.540
We're launching again !

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:31.030
Hurry up and resupply
the munitions !

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:32.290
Yes, sir !

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:37.070
How many did
you shoot down ?

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:37.630
Three.

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:38.510
How about you ?

00:07:38.510 --> 00:07:39.500
I've got three, too.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:40.210
Konev ?

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:41.080
Three.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:42.300
What's with you, Poplan ?

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:46.140
You've only taken one down, so it
looks like you're losing all by yourself.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:58.180
I don't mind losing, but I can't
stand letting other people make gains.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:00.720
People call that
"poor people's sour grapes."

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:03.900
I guess the Poplans didn't do a good job in
the personality development of their son.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:04.700
Shut up !

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:07.950
These pilots don't mean
to play with people's lives.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:12.510
They themselves offer up their own lives
to the transcendental ruler of the "game."

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:16.060
If an opponent of superior skills
comes before them someday...

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:20.040
...they will die in a fireball along
with their beloved fighter.

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:26.230
They believe it so, and they'd at least like
to live life cheerfully until that time comes.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:29.550
Since both sides are mixed
up on the battlefield...

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:32.180
...the Alliance should take
advantage of the opportunity...

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:35.790
...to retreat without allowing the
Empire to use the Thor Hammer.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:41.650
Chief General Officer, Admiral Greenhill, thought that, but it was difficult to actually pull that off.

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:44.580
To that end, they would have to pull their own fleets away from the enemy's.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:49.600
But if it goes wrong it could give the
Empire a chance to fire the Thor Hammer.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:53.360
The Alliance went to great lengths
to reorganize its fleet formation.

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:57.000
By deploying a portion of their fleets
toward the edge of the Corridor...

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:01.690
...they pushed the Imperial Fleets
inside the Thor Hammer's range...

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:03.790
...and then pulled back
their main units.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:08.390
This was done on Captain
Yang Wenli's recommendation...

00:09:08.390 --> 00:09:13.100
...but Admiral Greenhill also
successfully dealt more damage...

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:16.110
...to the Imperial Fleet
by attacking its left wing.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:20.100
In particular, Rear Admiral Holland's
fleet unit achieved tremendous results...

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:25.350
...and made a name for itself by swiftly
maneuvering near the enemy ships...

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:31.000
...to distract them, and then
concentrating its firepower on them.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:33.700
This was a tactical battle...

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:37.000
...and the result was enough to clear the
dishonor he had previously suffered...

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:39.250
...when his fleet had fled in chaos
upon the attack from Reinhard's fleet.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:43.850
Nonetheless, the Imperial Fleet did not suffer a
major debacle because of two young commodores...

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:48.200
...who had recently been
assigned to Iserlohn Fortress.

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:55.650
At this time, Commodore Oskar von Reuental was 27, and Commodore Wolfgang Mittemeyer was 26.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:59.670
They each had only 160 or so gunboats
and missile-ships under their commands...

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:04.570
...but their strategic positioning and swift
maneuvers brought about amazing results.

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:10.960
Of course, because of the large number differential they couldn't baffle the opposition too long.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:16.100
After confusing the enemy fleet to no end
for 50 minutes, the two quickly retreated.

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:20.100
One of the characteristics of
the 6th Battle of Iserlohn...

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:23.950
...was that young commanders in the Empire,
especially those under the age of 30...

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:26.650
...each garnered accolades for their accomplishments making names for themselves.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:31.100
Among the older commanders, in a manner becoming to his rank and reputation...

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:34.700
...Admiral Willebald Willem von Merkatz
was about the only one who performed.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:36.290
What is General
Headquarters doing ?

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:41.960
The rebels who call themselves the
Alliance can't afford to fight here forever !

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:45.870
All we have to do is take a portion of our
fleet and seal off their escape route !

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:49.640
Even if we just pretend to do something like
that, they'll panic and rush their withdrawal !

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:51.010
Why aren't we doing that ?

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:52.390
Lord Reinhard...

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:54.980
Kircheis, I can't
stand it anymore.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:58.300
Whether they like it or not, I'll
send a proposal to Headquarters.

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:00.770
Don't worry.

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:02.690
I'll choose my
words carefully.

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:04.830
You could write
it for me if you like.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:10.870
Reinhard sent a proposal to the Chief
Commander, Fleet Admiral Muckenberger.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:14.700
As he promised Kircheis, he followed
format and etiquette to the letter...

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.900
...but once the Commander
read it, he was enraged.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.470
That smartass blond brat !

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:22.000
He has the balls to voice
his opinions to his superior !

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:25.210
If he'd just stay quiet and follow orders,
he wouldn't have caused any stir !

00:11:25.690 --> 00:11:31.340
This may have possibly been the first time that Muckenberger was conscious of Reinhard's presence.

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:36.700
But because Muckenberger was not as incompetent as Reinhard's prejudices made him out to be...

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:40.400
...he had to admit that the
proposal was an effective strategy.

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:44.390
Therefore, Muckenberger decided to
settle the matter through a sly measure.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:49.350
I will inform you of the response from the
Chief Commander in regards to your proposal.

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:52.700
While he acknowledges the merit of your strategy, he questions whether it can be realized or not.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:57.350
Therefore, if you yourself feel confident enough to be responsible for carrying out the plan....

00:11:57.350 --> 00:12:00.800
...Headquarters will provide you
with sufficient support to this end.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:01.760
That's all.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:03.000
What will you do ?

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:05.460
They're basically saying,
"Do it yourself."

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:06.930
Are you going to do it ?

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:08.750
What do you
think we should do ?

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:10.640
We should do it, Lord Reinhard.

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:12.770
You think as I do.

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:18.410
I accept the mission.

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:22.650
Okay.

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.110
Let him do it.

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:26.750
If he fails, we'll
just think of other plans.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:31.670
Thus, many circumstances led
Muckenberger to make the decision...

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:38.250
...giving Reinhard an opportunity to shine and bringing about the end of the 6th Battle of Iserlohn.

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:44.310
The stance of the Alliance
was becoming more passive.

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:49.850
As their attacks between December 7th and 8th failed their mainstream staffers began to say...

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:52.920
...that they should retreat
before suffering fatal damage.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.590
Captain Yang recommends withdrawal.

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:00.310
According to the plan he
submitted the other day...

00:13:00.310 --> 00:13:02.340
Wait a minute, Admiral.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:06.690
The way you say it, Captain Yang had
already been thinking about a pull-back plan.

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:07.790
Is that right ?

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:09.200
Yes.

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:13.400
Six years ago, he succeeded
in withdrawing from El Facil.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:17.600
This time around, too, I think we
can rely on his strategic capabilities.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:22.480
Many people say that what
happened at El Facil was a fluke.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:26.550
Did you consider that point ?

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:28.050
I did.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:31.410
And I'm not recommending his proposal
without having closely examined it.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:36.140
But in this battle, he has demonstrated
many flashes of his tactical brilliance again.

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:38.000
But...

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:41.810
I report that a unit of the Imperial Fleet,
numbering approximately 2,200 to 2,500...

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:44.520
...has departed Iserlohn Fortress
bypassing our fleet...

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:48.210
...and is about to position itself behind
us to cut off our escape route.

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:52.110
This doesn't look good.

00:13:52.110 --> 00:13:54.800
Did Captain Yang
foresee this predicament ?

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:57.850
It was certainly among the
predictions he submitted.

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:06.530
By 22:00 on December 9th, the casualties
on both sides had reached 300,000.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.850
But if the Thor Hammer
had been used...

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:11.430
...the casualties on the Alliance side
would have been much higher...

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:14.250
...and those of the
Empire side much lower.

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:19.250
Therefore, if the Alliance returned home safely at his point the battle would be considered a success...

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:22.280
...and Lobos would most likely be
commended for his command abilities.

00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:27.070
Lobos can't be blamed if he made such calculations on his self-interest formula at that point.

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:28.300
All right.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.680
We'll prepare for withdrawal.

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:33.250
Regardless of Lobos's decision...

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:35.470
...the front-line commanders of each
Alliance unit had only one concern...

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:38.710
...to shoot down the opposition
right in front of them.

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:43.280
And as if to challenge them, Reinhard's
fleet showed up right in their face.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:45.700
I declare to all ships.

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:49.340
Follow my orders at all costs.

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:53.610
Follow only my commands to the letter
and make sure you execute them as ordered.

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:55.660
You have no other option.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:57.870
You must make a clear note of it.

00:14:57.870 --> 00:15:02.430
In other words, he's saying he's the only one
who knows how to get us all home alive...

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:04.870
...so we have to
listen to him, right ?

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:06.140
What should we do ?

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:08.780
Under the circumstances, we
can't afford to sabotage him.

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:11.060
I guess we'll have
to do as he says.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.320
But are we going to be okay ?

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:15.070
There's no point in
worrying about it.

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:18.250
Well, our commander is
incredibly good looking...

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:20.720
...so let's just hope his
brain is as good as his looks.

00:15:22.340 --> 00:15:25.000
Reinhard's real aim was to pretend
to wade through the melee area...

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:28.050
...on his way to cut off the
Alliance's escape route.

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:31.110
To this end, he did not engage in combat
with the Alliance ships on each side...

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:36.190
...and as he found the thinnest areas, he swiftly
moved his fleet to thread through those areas.

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:38.850
Naturally, the Alliance detected
such moves by Reinhard's fleet...

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:42.940
...and in order to annihilate this "cunning" enemy fleet the Alliance ships rushed in toward him.

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:43.710
Don't lose them.

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:44.360
Go get them !

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:49.510
As Reinhard concentrated fire on the first
wave of the Alliance ships, annihilated them...

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:51.600
...and then evaded
the second wave...

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:55.600
...the Alliance ships began a frenzied pursuit of this small fleet like an enraged man.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:57.460
This isn't good.

00:15:57.460 --> 00:16:01.420
A fleet of only 2,000 ships isn't
capable of cutting off our escape route.

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:03.030
This is a decoy.

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:08.470
The Empire's aim is to separate
our fleet from their fleet.

00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:11.980
But a fleet of 2,000 is too
small even for a decoy.

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:15.430
Isn't it a selfish move by someone
who is hastening for personal glory ?

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:22.150
Yeah, it most likely can't get past our
fleet's attack and will collapse right there.

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:25.900
It may be a selfish move after all, but
this combination of strategic creativity...

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:28.340
...pretending like he's
cutting off our escape route...

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:34.040
...and the tactical skill, to swiftly wade through
the chaotic battlefield, is highly unusual.

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:38.600
Moreover, he understands the psychological
weakness of a large fleet perfectly well.

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:42.780
For a large fleet, there's no bigger humiliation
than to be baffled by a much smaller fleet.

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:47.600
When that "humiliation" clouds the saner
judgement of the commanding personnel...

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:50.080
...that might become the trigger
for the debacle of the larger fleet.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:54.750
For this situation, Yang
did have a solution...

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:58.010
...to maintain the melee situation till the fleets get outside the Thor Hammer's range...

00:16:58.010 --> 00:17:02.150
...then separate the fleets there and retreat at maximum speed.

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:05.250
Yang submitted his second
proposal to Fleet Admiral Lobos...

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:08.730
...with an earnestness that
surprised even himself.

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:11.250
But in the end, Lobos
rejected this proposal...

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:14.390
...and did not stop the fleet
from pursuing Reinhard's unit.

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:16.930
They're coming
after us, Kircheis.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:18.710
They fell right into our trap.

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:21.720
I hope our fleet will
retreat as planned.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:28.770
If someone who yearns for glory pursues the
enemy fleet the Thor Hammer cannot be used.

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:33.910
Our tiny unit will be isolated in the middle of the
larger enemy fleet and we'll risk getting decimated.

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:39.610
The one in charge of the front line right
now is Merkatz, I think, and he's not flashy...

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:45.190
...but his skills are dependable and he probably has the judgment and insight to understand all this.

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:45.870
But...

00:17:46.780 --> 00:17:52.030
If he isn't as capable as I believe his
incompetence will save the Goldenbaum Dynasty.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.990
That statement was
more than just sarcasm.

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:59.850
After all, Reinhard was fighting
to topple the Goldenbaum Dynasty.

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:05.080
But unaware of such intentions, the
Imperial Fleet helped out the future usurper...

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:08.700
...by retreating while the Alliance's
command mechanisms were still in chaos.

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:10.080
Good.

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:12.810
We'll continue to engage in combat
and separate the enemy ships further.

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:23.330
It's okay to pursue that fleet, as it'll be
a chance for us to pull out of Iserlohn.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:30.200
But unless we remain close to the enemy units,
we'll become the Thor Hammer's targets.

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:33.500
We have to continue to engage in combat
and drag the enemy units with us.

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:36.510
There's nothing
I can do here.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:43.250
But in reality, the ones being dragged
along were the Alliance ships.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:48.800
Using such a small unit of about 2,000 ships,
he's baffling a large number of Alliance ships...

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:51.100
...while keeping
at close distance.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.850
Is he a petty trickster
with just enough talent...

00:18:52.850 --> 00:18:57.840
...to be in command of a small
fleet of 1,000 units, or maybe...?

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:58.950
Or perhaps...

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:00.900
...the commander of this unit...

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:05.660
...is the same one we failed to
capture last month in the corridor.

00:19:06.970 --> 00:19:11.100
I hope we won't be stingy with the number of ships as our chances may elude us in that case.

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:23.430
The Alliance ships went into a disorderly pursuit-battle without re-establishing its command system.

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:28.460
As silly as it may be, the fleet of 30,000 ships frantically pursued a unit of 2,000...

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:30.920
...took major damage from
the sharp counterattack...

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:34.190
...and became even more enraged and obsessed with annihilating it.

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:35.750
Don't let them get away !

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:37.840
Look at Iserlohn Fortress !

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:43.240
All units, move
upward immediately.

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.440
Toward the zenith,
at full speed !

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:46.420
Evacuate all the
way to the ceiling !

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:10.360
My God !  Several thousand ships
just evaporated in a second.

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:11.780
Here comes the second shot !

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:13.720
All units, retreat !

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:20.250
At 17:40 on December 10th,
the 6th Battle of Iserlohn ended...

00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:23.650
...with the complete withdrawal
of the Free Planets Alliance.

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:28.250
The casualties on the
Alliance side were 754,900...

00:20:28.250 --> 00:20:32.020
...and those of the
Imperial side were 368,800.

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:36.660
The Alliance not only failed in its
mission to capture Iserlohn Fortress...

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:39.200
...but their losses far
exceeded that of the Empire's.

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:43.050
The only solace was the strategic
self-satisfaction that derived from the fact...

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:46.600
...that they were on equal grounds with the
Empire before the Thor Hammer was fired...

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:50.030
...and in exchange for it, the equivalent
of the population of one city was lost.

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:54.360
Hey, do you want
a cup of coffee ?

00:20:55.500 --> 00:21:02.200
Because Julian makes such good tea,
the stuff here now tastes that much worse.

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:05.660
It's a good reason
to go home alive.

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:06.900
You should thank
him for that.

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:08.410
I guess so.

00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:10.480
You don't sound good.

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:11.900
What's the matter ?

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:15.390
Well, I was thinking if I had
a higher rank and more power...

00:21:15.390 --> 00:21:19.470
...I might have been able to decrease
the number of casualties a little bit.

00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:21.310
Maybe by just a few, but...

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:23.890
Did you know ?

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:26.330
People say you're a lucky man.

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:29.920
It was the case with what happened at
El Facil, too, but when people fail miserably...

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:35.050
...you fare a little better, and get
recognized and promoted for it.

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:38.760
This time around, I heard
you also did some good.

00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:41.590
When we return, you'll probably
be promoted to Commodore.

00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:45.550
Is that what
I really want ?

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:47.900
Do you want
something to drink ?

00:21:47.900 --> 00:21:51.290
To tell you the truth, my wife gave me
her treasured, homemade brandy...

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:53.660
...to celebrate our safe
return from battle.

00:21:54.690 --> 00:21:55.770
That sounds good.

00:21:55.770 --> 00:21:57.160
I'd like that.

00:21:57.160 --> 00:22:01.300
But in any case, the best wife to have
is the superior's daughter, isn't it ?

00:22:01.990 --> 00:22:02.930
Huh ?

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:11.250
Cheers !

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:13.950
Hey, Linz.

00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:15.750
Yes, Regimental Commander ?

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:18.070
There's a song about a
professional school student...

00:22:18.070 --> 00:22:20.390
...who parts with his lover
before a battle, isn't there ?

00:22:20.390 --> 00:22:21.570
Can you sing it for me ?

00:22:22.420 --> 00:22:23.890
"The Parting Song" ?

00:22:23.890 --> 00:22:25.560
I thought you hated it.

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:28.400
I still hate it.

00:22:30.780 --> 00:22:31.660
I understand.

00:22:31.660 --> 00:22:32.390
Then...

00:22:33.990 --> 00:22:43.030
Unable to bear the long parting...

00:22:43.030 --> 00:22:51.070
...I will drink from this wine glass.

00:22:52.570 --> 00:23:00.650
You are like a jewel.

00:23:00.650 --> 00:23:03.770
I will sing a parting song...

00:23:03.770 --> 00:23:07.950
...for you.

00:23:10.150 --> 00:23:14.300
Having woken up...

00:23:14.300 --> 00:23:18.440
...from the half-life of my dreams...

00:23:18.440 --> 00:23:22.680
...I think of the days...

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:27.230
...that have passed.

00:23:27.230 --> 00:23:35.230
The wine that absorbed your tears...

00:23:35.230 --> 00:23:43.220
...tastes bitter tonight.

00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:46.150
What ?

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:47.310
Is that all ?

00:23:47.630 --> 00:23:49.640
No, there's more.

00:23:49.640 --> 00:23:51.600
Then sing it, to the last.

00:23:54.040 --> 00:23:58.270
As I'm going to...

00:23:58.270 --> 00:24:02.140
...the field of death...

00:24:02.140 --> 00:24:06.550
...I can't help but hope...

00:24:06.550 --> 00:24:11.430
...for a tomorrow with you.

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:19.800
Putting my passion to rest...

00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:22.850
...I will sing...

00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:27.550
...for you.

00:24:31.640 --> 00:24:36.820
"Putting my passion to rest,
I will sing, for you," eh ?

00:24:38.560 --> 00:24:42.050
It's an old-fashioned,
cheap song.

00:24:42.050 --> 00:24:47.240
But why is it that
it strikes a chord so ?

00:24:51.830 --> 00:24:54.620
I guess it's because
I'm a cheap man.

00:24:56.620 --> 00:24:59.180
The Imperial Fleet was
excited by the victory.

00:24:59.180 --> 00:25:01.870
But Reinhard, despite having
played a key role in that victory...

00:25:01.870 --> 00:25:04.260
...simply couldn't bring himself
to be satisfied with it.

00:25:05.150 --> 00:25:09.070
We only relied on a weapon of
mass-destruction, the Thor Hammer.

00:25:09.070 --> 00:25:11.890
How can I be happy with such a cheap victory
that depended solely on such hardware ?

00:25:11.890 --> 00:25:15.250
If I were the commander, I would
have, without using the Thor Hammer...

00:25:15.250 --> 00:25:17.990
...defeated the rebels who
call themselves the Alliance.

00:25:20.050 --> 00:25:25.040
Kircheis, you've been looking at me for
a while, do you want to say something ?

00:25:25.040 --> 00:25:26.800
You look dissatisfied.

00:25:26.800 --> 00:25:28.950
Why do you think
I'm dissatisfied ?

00:25:28.950 --> 00:25:32.690
I was successful on the battlefield, and my
promotion to Vice Admiral is all but decided.

00:25:32.690 --> 00:25:34.460
My sister will
be happy, too.

00:25:34.960 --> 00:25:38.240
So why should
I look dissatisfied ?

00:25:38.240 --> 00:25:39.910
Did you know ?

00:25:39.910 --> 00:25:44.280
There will be another military action
against the rebels as soon as next year.

00:25:44.280 --> 00:25:49.140
Instead of allowing them to advance through
the Corridor, we'll be initiating it, it seems.

00:25:50.530 --> 00:25:53.610
That's quite an aggressive move
from Fleet Admiral Muckenberger.

00:25:53.610 --> 00:25:55.620
Is there a reason ?

00:25:55.620 --> 00:25:59.660
They say it's because the
casualties were low this time around.

00:25:59.660 --> 00:26:01.620
The casualties were low ?

00:26:01.620 --> 00:26:03.800
Since they didn't reach 400,000.

00:26:03.800 --> 00:26:08.100
Some 300,000 lives,
and their families.

00:26:08.100 --> 00:26:11.140
For the lineage aristocracy,
those are insignificant.

00:26:13.550 --> 00:26:17.070
Kircheis, I will not carry out
useless battles like this.

00:26:17.070 --> 00:26:20.060
I will not let
soldiers die meaninglessly.

00:26:20.060 --> 00:26:25.700
For us to get to our goal, we may
not be able to avoid casualties...

00:26:25.700 --> 00:26:28.710
...but I promise that I will not throw
away people's lives for futile causes.

00:26:28.710 --> 00:26:31.200
I know, Lord Reinhard.

00:26:31.200 --> 00:26:34.850
If you accomplish your
goal in the right way...

00:26:34.850 --> 00:26:39.920
...the lineage aristocracy can no
longer toy with commoners' lives.

00:26:39.920 --> 00:26:40.970
That's the way it will be.

00:26:40.970 --> 00:26:42.500
No, that's the
way I'll make it.

00:26:42.500 --> 00:26:46.800
In a not so distant
future, if you help me.

00:26:53.180 --> 00:26:59.680
In this galaxy, there are one hundred billion
stars, radiating one hundred billion lights...

00:26:59.680 --> 00:27:04.340
...and then there is one ambition,
radiating one single light.

00:27:01.010 --> 00:27:06.550
One Hundred Billion Stars, One Ambition

